Andhra Pradesh Advocates' Clerks' Welfare Fund Rules, 1992
to provide for annual inspection of the office;
(k)
to prepare annual administration report and statement of account on or after the 31st December of each year and
forward the same to the Government both in the Law Department and Finance and Planning (Finance Wing)
Department;
(l)
to authorise the Secretary to meet all incidental expenses and for providing for imprest money and the like;
(m)
to allocate funds for different heads of expenditure under these rules for each financial year;
(n)
to quantify:—
(i)
the Death Benefit to the surviving member or members of the family of the deceased Advocates' clerks;
(ii)
to grant to the indigent and disabled Advocates' Clerks;
(o)
to decide the person or persons to whom the "Death Benefit" should be given;
(p)
to call for the information and details as may be necessary from the concerned Advocates' Clerks' Association and the
members of the family of the deceased Advocates' clerks;
(q)
to make necessary enquiries, if required before taking decision under these rules;
(r)
to provide financial or other assistance to any Advocate's Clerk affected on account of any natural or unforeseen
circumstances;
(s)
to formulate and implement any further or other scheme or schemes for the benefit of Advocates' Clerks.
